From: Benjamin Bruun <bb@onomondo.com>
Subject: [PATCH] skeletons: drop the XML tag and, with ASN_DISABLE_NAMES, the name fields

XER is never built, so the xml_tag field of asn_TYPE_descriptor_t goes in every
build (constr_TYPE.h now requires ASN_DISABLE_XER_SUPPORT). ASN_DISABLE_NAMES
removes the name fields of the descriptor and member tables; it changes the
layout, so it must be the same in every unit, and it refuses asn1c debug output,
which reads the fields directly. Initialisers go through ASN_TYPE_NAME() and
ASN_MEMBER_NAME(); the XER, print and PER code that still reads a name, none of
which runs, goes through ASN_NAME_OF(), which gives "" without the field. The
skeleton descriptors drop their XML tag line and wrap their names the same way.
---
diff --git a/src/ipa/libasn/ANY.c b/src/ipa/libasn/ANY.c
--- a/src/ipa/libasn/ANY.c
+++ b/src/ipa/libasn/ANY.c
@@ -49,8 +49,7 @@ asn_TYPE_operation_t asn_OP_ANY = {
 	0	/* Use generic outmost tag fetcher */
 };
 asn_TYPE_descriptor_t asn_DEF_ANY = {
-	"ANY",
-	"ANY",
+	ASN_TYPE_NAME("ANY")
 	&asn_OP_ANY,
 	0, 0, 0, 0,
 	ASN_ENC_CONSTRAINTS(0, 0, asn_generic_no_constraint)	/* No constraints */
